# tests/i18n/BASELINE-CHANGES.rust: every intended change to the Dutch (or other frozen) text of the Rust host
# against 3b898e6, one exact key per line with a reason (contracts C3; plan.md ground rules).
# Checked by python3 -B tools/i18n/drift_rust.py. Two kinds of line, tab-separated, five fields:
#
#   host/src/<file>  <ordinal>  <sha256[:16]>  <replacement>  <reason>
#       a literal of tests/i18n/rust-frozen-all.tsv (path, ordinal and sha prefix exactly as listed there) that is
#       changed or removed without a catalogue row that rebuilds it; <replacement> names what took its place
#       (a catalogue key, "-" for nothing).
#   key:<catalogue key>  -  -  <old text or "-">  <reason>
#       a catalogue row whose Dutch text is new ("#@ new" rows, a plural .one form adopted under D-G1a, …).
#
# Round 2: each agent writes tests/i18n/BASELINE-CHANGES.rust-r2<x> in the same format; the coordinator merges.
#
# GE1b (round 1)
# C4/D-G6 native window titles: Dutch titles where 3b898e6 showed English in both languages (GE0c F2). Their ten
# key:window.title.* lines went with host/i18n/window.tsv in the no-WebKit stage (HOST-CORE): the native apps title
# their own windows; Task Manager's names of Default apps and the Installer are key:sysmon.ownApp.* (below)
# English titles that changed (the other seven 3b898e6 titles are the en of their window.tsv row: '#@ … en' lines)
host/src/window.rs	33	75304cf77db08b6e	window.title.alles	English-only native title 'Everything' in both languages (GE0c F2): now per kind in nl and en, re-applied on a switch (C4, D-G6); its en value is window.tsv's; en is Alles (D-G5)
host/src/window.rs	42	4532a8993d7c3965	window.title.pickerOpen	English-only picker title 'File selection': now Openen/Opslaan als/Map kiezen per picker mode, as the UI's picker title (C4); only a file-portal caller (another app) keeps its own title, Win11's own shell.pickFile callers get the mode title so it follows a switch (GE1b fix, review m3)
host/src/window.rs	45	f5000e099f97f0ae	window.title.installer	English-only native title 'App installer' in both languages (GE0c F2): now per kind in nl and en, re-applied on a switch (C4, D-G6); its en value is window.tsv's; en as the UI's frame title: App Installer
