# WebKit removal (HOST-UPDATE): the post-upgrade check and the compatibility check name GTK 4 (native shell and apps)
key:update.part.gtk4	-	-	-	new Windows Update host text: part label of libgtk-4-1, libgraphene-1.0-0 and libpango-1.0-0 (post_upgrade.rs PARTS, compat.rs part_of), the same in both languages
# no-WebKit stage (HOST-CORE): the host's WebKit GUI path, the WebKit picker window, the WebKit-only backend calls and
# GPU switches are gone; the apps are the native GTK 4 programs (win11-gtk-<kind>), the portal starts the native picker
key:sysmon.ownApp.defaultapps	-	-	Default apps	Task Manager's name of Default apps: was window.tsv's window.title.defaultapps (C4, the nl native title Standaard-apps), moved to sysmon.tsv when window.tsv went with the WebKit windows
key:sysmon.ownApp.installer	-	-	App installer	Task Manager's name of the Installer: was window.tsv's window.title.installer (C4, the nl native title App-installatieprogramma), moved to sysmon.tsv when window.tsv went with the WebKit windows
key:core.nativeAppMissing	-	-	Win11 voor GNOME: {path} ontbreekt; de WebKit-versie van de app start.	no WebKit fallback any more: a GUI launch without win11-gtk-<kind> names the missing binary and the fix (reinstall WinPoint) and exits 127; the portal says the same for a missing win11-gtk-explorer
